                        "sense_id": "c06b0966-5b80-3514-a463-689a4daae126",
                        "entry_id": "12b42e9e-f2a7-3df0-9404-5701551eb310",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Synonym of melomaniac."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "602672bf-6318-4176-bcea-11f143b7f728",
                                "sense_id": "c06b0966-5b80-3514-a463-689a4daae126",
                                "text": "Monsieur de Rochetaillée was a melomane. He thought of nothing, cared for nothing but music. It was the passion of his life; he could not live without music and musicians."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6c40229f-3938-43d6-b8b5-30b3d37d08f5",
                                "sense_id": "c06b0966-5b80-3514-a463-689a4daae126",
                                "text": "But what was even more important to Monet’s eventual success in devising landscape images that attracted music-modeled appreciation like Silvestre’s is the fact that the melomanes among the younger painters of the 1860s had not produced anything like a consistent painting practice modeled on music."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3d5dfe2c-c165-4133-b53b-44c86bcdc36b",
                                "sense_id": "c06b0966-5b80-3514-a463-689a4daae126",
                                "text": "But music in Tarantino is also part of a larger sonic obsession that stresses the acoustic impact of dialogue, noise, atmosphere, and effects—Tarantino is an audio[-]mane as much as a melomane."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
